<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sui dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sui</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sui dynasty reunified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 581–589 after centuries of division and ruled until 618. It built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a> but exhausted the country with costly wars, including campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. It was succeeded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a> describe Sui efforts to divide the Göktürks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sui dynasty" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ian Kiu · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cheui_Dynasty_581_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
